.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt ADJTIMEX 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm adjtimex ,
.Nm clock_adjtime
.Nd read or adjust the real-time clock's NTP state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/timex.h
.Ft int
.Fn adjtimex "struct timex *buf"
.Ft int
.Fn clock_adjtime "clockid_t clock" "struct timex *buf"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn adjtimex
reads the state the real-time clock keeps for NTP into
.Fa buf ,
after making the changes the bits of
.Fa buf->modes
ask for, and returns the clock's state:
.Dv TIME_ERROR
while
.Dv STA_UNSYNC
is set, as it is from boot until a program clears it, and
.Dv TIME_OK
otherwise.
.Fn clock_adjtime
does the same for
.Fa clock ,
which must be
.Dv CLOCK_REALTIME .
.Pp
The modes are Linux's, and any but
.Dv ADJ_OFFSET_SS_READ
needs a privileged caller.
This clock has no slew: an offset of
.Dv ADJ_OFFSET ,
at most the half second Linux takes one to be, a single-shot adjustment of
.Dv ADJ_OFFSET_SINGLESHOT ,
and the offset of
.Dv ADJ_SETOFFSET
step the real time at once, so none is left in progress and
.Fa offset
reads 0.
.Dv ADJ_FREQUENCY ,
.Dv ADJ_MAXERROR ,
.Dv ADJ_ESTERROR ,
.Dv ADJ_TIMECONST ,
.Dv ADJ_TAI
and
.Dv ADJ_STATUS
are kept and read back but change nothing the clock does;
.Dv ADJ_NANO
and
.Dv ADJ_MICRO
choose the unit of
.Fa offset
and of
.Fa time.tv_usec .
The tick is the timer's 10000 microseconds, the precision 1 microsecond
and the tolerance Linux's 500 ppm.
.Pp
While
.Dv STA_UNSYNC
is clear, a privileged call that changes anything also copies the time,
rounded to the second, to the CMOS clock, at most once in 11 minutes, as
Linux's 11-minute mode does, so that the next boot starts from the time
an NTP daemon kept.
.Pp
The i386 system call numbers are 124 for
.Fn adjtimex
and 343 for
.Fn clock_adjtime ,
which take the 128-byte
.Vt struct timex
of 32-bit fields, and 405 for
.Fn clock_adjtime64 ,
which takes the 208-byte
.Vt struct __kernel_timex
of 64-bit fields that musl and glibc use.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The clock's state, or -1 with
.Va errno
set; the kernel returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
BusyBox's
.Xr adjtimex 1
prints the state, and its
.Xr ntpd 8
sets the clock through these calls and
.Xr clock_settime 2 .
The default suite's
.Pa tests/musl/callsmusl.c
reads the state and requires
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
of
.Dv CLOCK_MONOTONIC .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa buf
is not readable and writable.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Dv ADJ_TICK
asks for a tick other than 10000 microseconds, the fraction of
.Dv ADJ_SETOFFSET
is not under a second, or
.Fa clock
is not a clock.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
.Fa clock
is a clock other than
.Dv CLOCK_REALTIME .
.It Bq Er EPERM
A mode other than reading was asked for by a caller without privilege.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clock_settime 2 ,
.Xr gettimeofday 2
